 Provision of support to User Acceptance Testing and Operational Acceptance Testing activities; 
 Identification and following up of defects status in close collaboration with the development team; 
 Provision of support to developers in unit testing activities.
Your skills: 
 University Degree in IT with minimum 6 years of professional experience in various areas of software testing; 
 Minimum 4 years of experience in functional testing and 2 years in organizing user acceptance testing; 
 Minimum 1 year of experience reviewing requirements and defining acceptance criteria in multi-national or law enforcement projects; 
 Working experience of minimum 6 months with Palantir Government solutions and Visual Studio Team Foundation Server; 
 Knowledge of black box and white box testing, defect-based and experience-based testing as well as system integration testing; 
 Very good knowledge of formal reviews of requirements and definition of acceptance criteria; 
 Knowledge of scripting functional automated tests with HP QuickTest Professional using VBScript data migration testing, SQL and Linux is an asset; 
 Delivery of end-user trainings and presentation experience is advantageous; 
 ISTQB certification is desirable; 
 Fluency in both oral and written English.
